  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Leaching is often used if the ore is soluble in some suitable solvent. The ore of tin metal is cassiterite(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>). Cassiterite is readily soluble in alkali. The reaction is shown below.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Sn</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p></blockquote>",
